 production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east had moved to v2.3.0, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback once and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already existed, so I did not create a duplicate. Its summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call engineer:\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures.\n- Investigate the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.\n- Redeploying v2.3.1 would need change-manager approval, because it has never been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}